---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
const pageTitle = "About";
const pageDescription =
  "Richmann - Software Engineer x Product designer - designing clean, thouhtful user experiences and building the tech bringing those experiences to life.";
const ogURL = "https://richmnn.com/about";
const keywords =
  "Software Engineer, Product Designer, Web Design & Development, High-Performing Software, Web Development, Empathy in Design, Design and Code, User-Centered Design, User Experience (UX), Problem Solving, Technology & People, Tech & Creativity, Design Process, Development Skills, Design & Development Integration, Personal Growth & Development, Resilience in Tech, Professional Journey, Continuous Learning, Software Solutions, Tech Industry Insights, Technology for Real-World Impact, Lifelong Learning, Self-Improvement, Tech & Empathy, Building Better User Experiences, Work-Life Balance in Tech, Chelsea Football Fan, Anime Inspiration, Knowledge Acquisition, Personal Reflection.";
const gap = 16;
---

<BaseLayout
  pageTitle={pageTitle}
  pageDescription={pageDescription}
  ogURL={ogURL}
  keywords={keywords}
  gap={gap}
>
  <!-- Header -->
  <div class="w-full text-[16px]">
    <p class="italic text-tertiary">A little rant about me</p>
    <h1 class="text-primary font-mr font-semibold">What I do and why I care</h1>
  </div>

  <!-- Glimpse of my work -->
  <div
    class="w-full flex flex-col gap-[24px] text-[14px] font-semibold font-mr"
  >
    <hr />
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-[48px]">
      <h2 class="text-secondary">A glimpse at my work</h2>
      <div
        class="w-full h-[410px] bg-bgsecondary flex items-center justify-center"
      >
        <p class="text-tertiary text-[12px]">coming soon</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Extended About -->
  <div
    class="w-full flex flex-col gap-[24px] text-[14px] font-semibold font-mr"
  >
    <hr />
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-[48px]">
      <h2 class="text-secondary">Extended About</h2>
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-[24px] text-tertiary">
        <p>
          Hi again! It took me a while to figure out what I’d say here - and
          honestly, I almost didn’t. But I tried to keep it short so here goes.
          When you strip away the job titles, the design specs, and the code,
          I’m just a person. I’m a software engineer and product designer who’s
          spent quite some time learning how to create better tech and better
          products. But beyond that, I’m someone who enjoys the process of
          building things that solve real problems for real people.
        </p>
        <p>
          I always knew I wanted to be a software engineer primarily because I
          enjoy building systems. It’s not exactly the same with product design.
          Empathy wasn’t exactly my strong suit (still working on that!), but
          design interests me because it mixes creativity and problem-solving in
          ways that feel purposeful.
        </p>
        <p>
          Professionally, in relation to design I’m interested in figuring out
          why some products keep users coming back. Why are they more engaging?
          How can I replicate that in my own work? It's not just about design
          principles; it's about the science behind what makes users stay. And
          it’s only afterwards that development comes in. I find peace in building
          things - turning concepts into products that bring value to other
          people.
        </p>
        <p>
          I didn’t start in a fancy design studio or graduate from an IVY league
          university. It was more like late nights, a lot of self-doubt, a lot
          of reading, studying, and even more Google searches and ChatGPTing
          than I’d like to admit. But every challenge has pushed me forward.
          Every success & failure has taught me something new. And I am here
          today, a mix of creative and technical.
        </p>
        <p>
          Outside of work? Well, I’m pretty laid-back, but I do enjoy good food
          (and yes, I might even trade a friendship for an extra plate). I love
          reading (knowledge acquisition... anyone?). Big fan of football (Chelsea
          football club, and no, you can’t change my mind). Find me with
          Pinterest boards full of inspiration, a clean physical aesthetic,
          movies, anime, nature... yeah, good stuff. I’m still figuring it out,
          just like everyone else, but I’m committed to growing, learning, and
          getting 1% better each day - credit to Atomic Habits for teaching me that.
        </p>
        <p>
          This portfolio? It’s not just a bunch of work I’ve done; it’s a small
          extension of me. I’ve got plenty more to learn, but I’m always up for
          the next challenge. If you’re interested in working together or just
          want to say hello please don’t hesitate. In the words of someone I
          look up to - “My gratitude for the opportunity to be here now is
          larger than an html file can hold. You could be anywhere - and yet,
          you are here now.”
        </p>

        <p>
          <a
            href="/getintouch"
            class="underline text-primary hover:text-secondary">Reach out</a
          > to say hello if you’ve liked what you’ve seen. I’m always open to conversation.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
